1. able to analyze music and decide appropriate conducting patterns;
2. able to plan an effective choral/orchestral rehearsal with different approaches;
3. able to conduct music with healthy and relaxed body gestures;
4. able to express music and give clear non-verbal instructions with minimal movements;
5. able to self-evaluate his/her performance of a rehearsal or a concert.

By the end of the course, students will be expected to demonstrate the following skills and knowledge:

1. Fundamental understanding of issues and concepts related to the topical area under consideration;
2. Awareness of the relationship between the methodologies discussed and the respective critical or analytical implications;
3. Critical response to major scholarly publications and state of research of the topical area under consideration;
4. Ability to apply the concepts learnt to their own research.

By the end of the course, the student will be expected to:

1. Demonstrate a fundamental understanding of the compositional techniques introduced in the course;
2. Demonstrate creativity and originality in their own works, and the progressive development of a personal style;
3. Express self-reflective and informed judgments about their own compositions, compositional approaches and

creative ideas;
4. Have built a portfolio of compositions for small instrumental ensembles.

